      ":question/problem": "Find $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ given that $f(x,y)=7 \\arctan{\\left(y \\right)}- 7 x y^{2}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(7 \\arctan{\\left(y \\right)}- 7 x y^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(7 \\arctan{\\left(y \\right)})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(7 x y^{2}) \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\arctan{\\left(y \\right)})-7 x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y^{2}) \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{1}{y^{2} + 1}-7 x\\cdot 2 y \\\\  & =- 14 x y + \\frac{7}{y^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
