      ":question/worked-solution": "The notation ${f}_{y}$ denotes the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $y.$\n\nWe differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants.\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(7 x^{4} y+\\frac{x^{3}}{y^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(7 x^{4} y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x^{3}}{y^{3}}) \\\\  & =7 x^{4}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)+x^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{y^{3}}) \\\\  & =7 x^{4}\\cdot (1)+x^{3}\\cdot (- \\frac{3}{y^{4}}) \\\\  & =7 x^{4} - \\frac{3 x^{3}}{y^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
